# 6. Turnaround scorecard

The board should review a concise weekly and monthly scorecard.

## Financial

- Monthly EBITDA and EBIT;
- Operating cash flow and cash burn;
- Contract and service-line contribution;
- Gross margin on new bookings;
- Restructuring cash spent versus approved amount;
- Working capital, unbilled revenue, and overdue receivables;
- Return on invested capital for the retained core.

## Commercial

- Book-to-bill;
- Backlog value and expected margin;
- Renewal rate;
- Price realization;
- Win rate at or above target margin;
- Customer attrition;
- Pipeline quality;
- Cross-selling supported by verified group economics.

## Operational

- Productive technician utilization;
- First-time-fix rate;
- Schedule adherence;
- Overtime and subcontractor expense;
- Travel and mobilization cost;
- Rework and warranty cost;
- Project-estimate variance;
- Change-order recovery;
- Billing-cycle time.

## People and risk

- Critical-role retention;
- Leadership vacancies;
- Employee turnover and absence;
- Safety incidents;
- Quality failures and service penalties;
- Customer complaints;
- Legal, environmental, and regulatory exposures.

Reported improvement should exclude unsupported future savings and distinguish recurring results from temporary actions such as delayed maintenance or unpaid suppliers.

